<title>SOUTH KOREA: Kolon Ind 1996 net profit narrows.</title>
<headline>Kolon Ind 1996 net profit narrows.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	 (billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)			  798    vs 1,491</p>
<p>    Net				   10.1  vs    13.7</p>
<p>    Profit before tax		 12.6  vs    17.4</p>
<p>    Turnover			   936.6  vs   931.0</p>
<p>Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)</p>
<p>		common  (in cash)	8    vs     2</p>
<p>			  (in stock)  none    vs     2</p>
<p>	     preferred (in cash)     9    vs     3</p>
<p>			   (in stock) none    vs     2</p>
<p>    Extrodinary gain		   1.0  vs    13.3</p>
<p>    Divident payment		   late March</p>
<p>Note - Kolon Industries Inc is South Korea's second largest maker of nylon and polyester yarns. Its share capital rose to 17.3 million shares at the end of 1996 from 12.6 million at end-1995 due to dividend payments and rights issues.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
